# Build context for map-web/Dockerfile and packages/epic-map/Dockerfile, both of
# which build from the repository root because both resolve their dependencies
# through the root npm workspace and its single lockfile.
#
# map-api has its own .dockerignore and is built with map-api/ as its context,
# so nothing here applies to it.

.git
.github

# Installed inside the image from the lockfile, never copied in.
**/node_modules
**/dist

# Secrets. sample.env is the committed template and is safe to keep.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/sample.env

# Nothing either web build needs.
map-api
deployment
**/venv
**/coverage
**/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
# Test output only: map-web's tsc needs cypress/support, where cy.mount is declared.
**/cypress/screenshots
**/cypress/videos
**/*.log
